Z||000000||84fierotrevor||11-02-2001||04:55 AM||||well when i first got my fiero i was kinda skeptical and guess i guess the fiero has grown on me now i can't come home everyday without checking these forums <BR>and today i saw a fiero parked out side of fries electronics <BR>and people where looking at me funny cuss<BR>I SCREAMED HO00000LLY SHIIIIIT ITS A FIERO !! !and i walked around it slowly checking it all out like it was some kinda never before seen lamborgini prototype i just walked around looking at it for like 10 minutes in the parking lot looking in the window and checking out the little side scoop on the side and finnaly i left ha haha god it was sweet looking cuss i only seen two other fieros on the road since i purchesd mine and they where trashed to the ground and not taken care of....i wonder how long it will be tell i become so obbseased with fieros i will attack a guy that hasnt taken care of his fiero and bite him screaming fiero beater u hould jailed muther f@%*r ! * sigh Fieros are like a virus that gets ahold of u and slowly takes u over one day at a time.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Springtyme||11-02-2001||05:39 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 84fierotrevor:<BR><B>Fieros are like a virus that gets ahold of u and slowly takes u over one day at a time.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'll agree with that! Ever since Eric gave me a ride in his I wanted one. Then when he started doing the engine swap and it wasn't drivable anymore I was rather upset, so it was time to get my own! The other day I pulled into Strauss Auto (after I had raced, and beat a Ford Probe) and I parked next to an 84 SE (I think) that was VERY well taken care of. I even waited around a little bit to see who owned it. They had their lights on and I thought of going in and having them page it so I could see who owned it, but I was too chicken. I hope their battery wasn't dead....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Anyway, I let Eric take my car into work this morning because he was running late and his jeep gets him there a lot slower. I miss it already, but I did get this in an email from him... "When I pulled into the parking lot, everyone was looking at it. I got out of the car and one of the guys I work with asked if I had neon lights under the fenders. I showed hime your valve stem lights, he hought they where neat." <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Springtyme.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000002||stimpy||11-02-2001||05:58 AM||||Here for your utilisation, absolutely free of charge, is the following basic punctuations. They are nothing fancy; no semicolons or parentheses (as the use of such may be beyond your grasp), just some basic periods and commas. You will find that using these will present you with an opportunity to actually break up the ramblings in your head into what might be a sembelance of cohesive thought. I encourage you to cut and paste these if necessary, and I'm sure with some practice you will find them to be great fun. We, your audience, will be entirely greatful.<P>For your consideration, <BR>The Period- <B>.</B> These go at the end of what is called a <B>sentance</B>. A sentance is a complete cohesive thought. I know it's a stretch, but I'm sure with practice you can manage. <P>The Comma- <B>,</B> These go inside a sentance,and come in handy when you want to keep two cohesive thoughts "buddies". At this stage in your development, you may even choose to use the comma interchangebly with the period. <B>That's OK!</B> I would be an improvement to be sure. <P>Anyhow, in response to your post. Yes, Fieros are pretty, aren't they?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||avengador1||11-02-2001||10:41 AM||||I looked up "sentance" in my Webter's dictionary. Didn't find it. Found "sentence". The fourth definition is: "a grammatically self-contained speech unit consisting of a word or a syntactically related group of words that expresses an assertion a question, a command, a wish, or an exclamation, that is written usu. etc..."<BR>Im sure there aren't too many English mayors on this forum and I don't claim to be one. I notice that we all make mistakes once in a while while posting. I believe this is because we are in a hurry to get our posts' on. I guess my point is whether this is being done on purpose or by accident, it should be ignored. Trying to correct someone makes for a more negative forum and could raise ill feelings. Thank you, this is just a suggestion. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||TRiAD||11-02-2001||11:21 AM||||Between "I would be a major imporvement", "sentance", and "English mayors", I don't know who's funnier!<P>Thanks guys!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0NgAlAL0S2vLvViYU9P7uloj72fLFTqfz59trng8I7AOG7hGCvfk6WP96n!gnOaEUAvooy1kUoWucv7BJ7L5EWg/temp-sig.gif">    <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
